# Build-time configuration for `npm run build`. Vite loads this automatically
# for a production build, so the correct bundle is what you get by default.
#
# Created 2026-09-02. This was set nowhere in the repo and had to be typed on
# the command line every time. It never was: EVERY shipped bundle carried only
# the DEFAULT_ADMIN_EMAILS fallback, so admin@noguessworksystems.com was admin
# on the backend and NOT admin in the UI — every admin affordance hidden from
# the one account that needed them. Checked back through three earlier bundles;
# admin@ had never appeared in any of them.
#
# NOT A SECRET. This list already ships inside the bundle by design, and
# ui/src/config/admin.js says so plainly: it is a convenience gate, never a
# security boundary. Every privileged action is authorised server-side against
# NGW_ADMIN_EMAILS, which lives only in the Render dashboard.
#
# Keep in sync with NGW_ADMIN_EMAILS on the server. Both REPLACE rather than
# append, so listing one address silently revokes the others.
VITE_NGW_ADMIN_EMAILS=admin@noguessworksystems.com
